# Verification-First Rule

After implementing changes, always run a verification pass before finalizing.

## Required checks
- Validate correctness, regressions, and edge cases in changed scope.
- Run relevant lint/typecheck/tests when feasible.
- Identify missing tests and risky assumptions.
- Propose better alternatives when current approach is fragile or overly complex.

## Response requirements
- Present findings first (Critical -> Important -> Suggestion).
- Include why it is a problem and a concrete fix path.
- If no findings, explicitly mention residual risks and untested areas.

Use the `verification-reviewer` skill behavior when performing this pass.
